<div class="exercise-info">
    <h1>Exercise Name: Seated Leg Extension (Standard / Neutral Foot Placement)</h1>
    <u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u>


This 3D anatomical visualization demonstrates the standard Seated Leg Extension exercise with a neutral foot placement ("toes up"). The video highlights the quadriceps muscle group in glowing colors to show how keeping your feet parallel and pointing straight up evenly targets the middle and overall upper thighs (Rectus Femoris and overall quad heads) throughout the extension.
 Exercise Name: Seated Leg Extension (Standard / Neutral Foot Placement)
 Target Muscles: Overall Quadriceps (Rectus Femoris, Vastus Lateralis, Vastus Medialis, Vastus Intermedius)
 Secondary Muscles: None (Pure isolation exercise)

</div></div>
<pre>
    <h1>How to Perform (Step-by-Step)</h1>

 <u><b><h4>Machine Setup</h4></b></u>: Adjust the back pad so your lower back rests firmly against it and your knee joint aligns with the machine's pivot point. Position the lower pad so it sits comfortably against your shins, just above the ankles.
 <u><b><h4>Foot Position</h4></b></u>: Point your feet straight up ("toes up") in a neutral, parallel position. Keep your knees aligned with your toes.
 <u><b><h4>Lifting Phase</h4></b></u>: Hold the side handles firmly to lock your hips into the seat. Exhale as you extend your legs upward in a smooth, controlled motion until your legs are fully extended (without forcefully locking out the knees).
 <u><b><h4>Lowering Phase</h4></b></u>: Pause for a brief second at the top, squeeze your quads, and inhale as you slowly lower the weight back down to the starting position.



<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

 <b>◉Balanced Quad Activation:</b> Standard foot placement distributes tension evenly across all four quad heads rather than over-emphasizing inner or outer thigh sections.
 <b>◉Pure Quad Isolation:</b> Directly builds leg extension strength without fatigue in your lower back or glutes.
 <b>◉Easy Progression:</b> Allows straightforward tracking of progressive overload for building defined, symmetrical thighs.



<h1>Recommended Sets & Reps</h1>

| Goal | Sets | Reps | Rest |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Muscle Building (Hypertrophy) | 3 – 4 | 10 – 12 | 60 – 90 seconds |
| Endurance / Tone | 3 – 4 | 12 – 15 | 45 – 60 seconds |
| Strength | 3 – 4 | 8 – 10 | 90 seconds |

Keep the tempo steady—lower the weight over 2 to 3 seconds instead of dropping it quickly to keep constant tension on the muscle.
